1|0@zen^1440545882#cufo2sy:mujushingyo$:"Doing Zen" means "absorption in oneness and absorption in unified activity." (Hui-Neng) It also means "giving rise to a mind that does not abide anywhere." (The Diamond Sutra) It also means "to look at one's nature inwardly." (Hui-Neng) It also means "making the mind empty like space" (Pai-Chang), "learning to halt the concept-forming activities of your own mind," "keeping the mind motionless whether sitting, walking, standing or lying down," "calming mental functions and forgetting views," and "not clinging to anything." (Huang-Po) It is also "detaching from form" (Layman Pang) &gt;When the feelings of judgments of intellectual consciousness are ended, only then can you see through. -Yuanwu &gt;When body and mind achieve spontaneity, the Way is reached and Mind is understood. -Huang-Po 
